  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the quotient rule and put the numerator and denominator under separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{pq}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{pq}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to remove the radical $\\sqrt{pq}$ from the denominator. To do this, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{pq},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{pq}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{pq}}{\\sqrt{pq}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{11pq}}{(\\sqrt{pq})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{11pq}}{pq}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
